select 18, v.verse, v.sanskrit, null, null, v.title, v.application, $q$Sanskrit: moolam via Heritage IITK (public domain). Recitation: Swami Brahmananda, CC BY-SA 4.0, Heritage IITK. English: Swami Sivananda. Hindi: Swami Tejomayananda. Translations via Heritage IITK with permission. Title and daily note: AI-drafted. Draft — pending editorial review$q$, '{}'::text[]
from (values
  (1, $q$अर्जुन उवाच
संन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम्।
त्यागस्य च हृषीकेश पृथक्केशिनिषूदन॥$q$, $q$Renunciation and abandonment$q$, $q$Arjuna asks how giving up action differs from giving up its fruits.$q$),
  (2, $q$श्री भगवानुवाच
काम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः।
सर्वकर्मफलत्यागं प्राहुस्त्यागं विचक्षणाः॥$q$, $q$Two ways of letting go$q$, $q$Krishna distinguishes renouncing desire-driven acts from releasing the rewards of action.$q$),
  (3, $q$त्याज्यं दोषवदित्येके कर्म प्राहुर्मनीषिणः।
